 P5 Drills: DrillsPage owns collection/preset/mode presentation after guarded later-entry transfer. CHG-057 DrillCard shares its icon/text-column/action structure with PracticeCatalog; catalog chip strips are removed while Configure/help retain sequence details. The custom editor remains an independent native subtree until its P5 UI migration, retaining invalid drafts, selection and handlers. Shared RetainedNode also owns Settings file/preview lifetimes; explicit non-layout structural classes preserve existing CSS sibling contracts. PageHeading now supplies the unchanged numbered-title structure for Settings/Learn/Live Listen/Drills, while its default About/Contact contract remains intact. Free saved-preset use/edit and Full-only creation/simulation are verified through the actual mounted page.
 
 P5 custom editor: CustomDrillEditor shares complete prerender and live fields; the existing feature owns private steps/permissions/save and the stable form submit/visibility host. A typed field renderer owns caption/step/action presentation after transfer; native child mutation remains only in startup fallback. The original native behavior was characterized before extraction, then the same scenarios run against native and React renderers: Free saved edits, Full creation, repeats/reorder/limits, rejected saves, cancel/reset and stale permissions/profiles. Draft, dropdown, validation, focus and retry behavior remain intact. History boundary analysis is offloaded to [ownership notes](../project/react-refactor/history-ownership-notes.md).
+
+
+CHG-053: one pure `features/live-listen/readiness.ts` policy distinguishes valid-gun navigation from trained capture. `renderListeningReadiness` updates Home, Drills, Live Listen and shared chrome through existing native/React ports. LiveListenPage owns reason-copy metadata and described-by/status semantics; current gun counts and operation locks remain main/controller-owned. Timing controllers construct once only after a gun exists; native onboarding/restore/reset/background paths work without them. No capture API, matching threshold, data schema or renderer ownership change.
